Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates hands-on design of a real-time RAG system, including multi-embedding chunking, multi-stage retrieval, and data freshness in production-like conditions.

Key Concepts
- Dual-embedding chunking
- Vector DB indexing and cosine search
- Cross-encoder reranking
- Streaming updates and TTL pruning
- Latency targets and observability

Code Example
```javascript
async function retrieve(query) {
  const eSent = await embed(query, 'sentence');
  const eSect = await embed(query, 'section');
  const topSent = vectorDB.search(eSent,  topK);
  const topSect = vectorDB.search(eSect, topK);
  // fuse and rerank
  return rerank(topSent, topSect, query);
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and improve retrieval quality in production?
- How would your design adapt if the vector DB spans multiple regions with different latencies?

## Why This Is Asked

To assess the ability to design policy-aware, scalable agent orchestration that handles multi-tenant data isolation and observability.

## Key Concepts

- LangChain agent orchestration with AutoGen planning
- Private APIs and data catalog integration
- Policy enforcement and tenant isolation
- End-to-end traceability, auditing, and failure handling
- Resilience patterns: retries, backoff, circuit breakers

## Code Example

```javascript
async function plan(request) {
  const { userId, tenantId, dataScope } = request;

  const policyResult = await policyEngine.check({ tenantId, dataScope });
  if (!policyResult.allowed) {
    throw new Error('Access denied: policy violation');
  }

  const catalogResult = await dataCatalog.query({ tenantId, dataScope });
  const apiResult = await privateApi.fetch({ tenantId, dataScope });

  await auditLogger.log({
    tenantId,
    userId,
    steps: [policyResult, catalogResult, apiResult],
    traceId: uuid()
  });

  return { data: apiResult, traceId: traceId };
}
```

This flow ensures tenant-scoped policies are enforced at entry, each component call is traced, and failures are handled with compensating transactions or graceful degradation.

## Why This Is Asked
Examines practical system design for multilingual retrieval at scale, including chunking, embeddings, vector storage, and data provenance.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual embeddings and cross-language retrieval
- Chunking strategies and token budgets
- Incremental updates and data provenance
- Observability, metrics, and testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-flow wiring
async function retrieve(query) {
  const e = embed(query);
  const chunks = vectorDB.search(e, topK=5);
  const ranked = rerank(chunks, query);
  return ranked.map(c => ({id: c.id, text: c.text, source: c.source}));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test update propagation for edited docs?
- How would you measure latency under burst traffic?

## Why This Question Matters
Provides a practical, beginner-friendly approach to assessing grounding, code fidelity, and relevance for a developer assistant across private documentation corpora with versioning support.

## Key Concepts
- Grounding responses to exact doc version and section
- Detection of code block hallucinations
- Metrics: precision@1, grounding coverage, and citation drift

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal runner skeleton
const prompts = loadPrompts('prompts-50.json');
prompts.forEach(p => {
  const ans = model.ask(p);
  const grounded = verifyGrounding(ans, p.docVersion, p.section);
  const hallucinated = detectHallucinations(ans, p.docVersion);

  console.log(JSON.stringify({
    prompt: p.question,
    grounded,
    hallucinated,
    precisionAt1: computePrecision(ans, p.expectedEndpoints)
  }));
});
```
